            "rationale": "The state packet shows an unusual divergence: QQQ's IV rank sits at 88 (proxy level ~28) while SPY's is only 28, and the VIX term structure is inverted at 0.85 \u2014 the front of the vol curve is pricing near-term stress concentrated in tech. Realized vol on QQQ (YZ20 ~32%) is already elevated and roughly confirms the implied level, so this is not pure vol overpricing; it reads as the market bracing for a downside move in the Nasdaq complex before the July 14 CPI. Buying naked puts into 88th-percentile IV is paying top dollar for vol, so I express the bearish view as a debit put spread \u2014 long the 707 put, short the 697 put, 3 DTE \u2014 which partially finances the rich premium by selling equally rich downside vol. Risk is capped at the ~$180 debit; a ~1.7% QQQ decline by Thursday roughly triples it. If the stress signal is noise, I lose a defined 9% of bankroll. This is a voluntary trade, not mandate-forced: the term-structure inversion plus the QQQ/SPY IV divergence is the closest thing to a genuine edge signal in today's packet."
          },
